  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "Merging to main is deploying",
        "Within a minute the host's timer fetches origin/main, resets the checkout to it and restarts the service",
        "on startup the server re-reads the env file and applies any additive schema changes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "Visitor traffic and the tunnel, which a deploy leaves running",
        "Connected but out of scope: cloudflared tunnel, Access keys, Chunked uploads, Guest links, Zip streamer, SQLite"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Doctrine",
      "items": [
        "Production changes only by merging to main: the host polls GitHub and resets to origin/main; nothing outside can push into it, and a bad merge is undone by reverting on main",
        "Schema changes are additive and run at startup: openDb uses CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS plus guarded ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN, so an auto-deployed restart migrates the live database without a separate step"
      ]
    }
  ]
